From e895872655287e247d543a9e21ea0a4c21b5640d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:21:57 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 096/119] clk: samsung: exynos9810: Add read-only CMU_TOP and
 leaf CMUs

Add the Exynos9810 CMU blocks used so far next to CMU_CHUB: CMU_TOP
(shared PLLs), CMU_APM, CMU_CMGP (USI_CMGP, HSI2C), CMU_PERIC0/1 (USI,
UART), CMU_PERIS (MCT, watchdogs, TMU), CMU_FSYS0 (UFS, USB), CMU_DPU
and CMU_G3D (Mali).

The tables are generated from Samsung's CMUCAL data for S5E9810. These
CMUs are read-only for now: the PLLs have no rate tables, and all muxes
and dividers are CLK_MUX_READ_ONLY / CLK_DIVIDER_READ_ONLY, so the
reported rates are what the bootloader and the APM firmware set up.
Nothing is written to them unless clk_exynos9810.manual_gates=1 is
passed, which switches the gates of the leaf CMUs from hardware auto
gating to manual mode, forcing each of them on first. CMU_TOP, CMU_APM
and CMU_G3D are never switched: the APM firmware relies on the first
two, and the G3D gates follow the GPU power domain.

CMU_CHUB stays a writable CMU registered through
exynos_arm64_register_cmu(), as SPI21 has to set its USI divider. Its
DLL input now refers to the CMU_APM gate by its real name.

The register map was checked on SM-T570: every register the driver
reads can be read on a running system (reading undefined offsets in
the CMU space raises an SError; CMU_G3D stays accessible while the GPU
domain is off), and the computed rates match the values found by hand
during UFS and GPU bring-up: PLL_SHARED4 666.25 MHz, FSYS0 bus
333.125 MHz, UFS UniPro 166.5625 MHz, PLL_G3D 260 MHz.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
